**CSS‑only rotating card**

Below is a minimal example that shows how to create a “flip” card that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only CSS – no JavaScript required.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Basic reset & container ---------- */
body{
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center;
    height:100vh; margin:0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card wrapper (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper{
    width:260px; height:160px;
    perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Card itself (transition + backface hidden) ---------- */
.card{
    width:100%; height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition:transform .6s ease; /* smooth rotation */
}

.card:hover{
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* flip around Y axis on hover */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.front, .back{
    position:absolute;
    width:100%; height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide backside when turned away */
    border-radius:10px;
    box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    overflow:hidden;
}

.front{
    background:#fff;
    display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#333;
}

.back{
    background:#4a90e2;
    color:#fff;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* start rotated so it's hidden initially */
    display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center;
    font-size:1.5rem;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="front">Front side</div>
        <div class="back">Back side</div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | The page is centered and has a neutral background. |
| **2** | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` creates a 3‑D context for its child. |
| **3** | `.card` holds both sides and transitions its `transform`. On hover it rotates 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| **4** | Both `.front` and `.back` are absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the face that’s turned away from the viewer. The back face starts rotated 180°, so it’s invisible until the parent flips. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add images inside `.front` and `.back`. You can also change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip, or adjust the `perspective` value to make the effect more or less pronounced.
